      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hi, I'm a chemistry teacher in London. I'm currently drafting a handout for my Year 11 students regarding the biochemistry of Allium vegetables. \n\nCould you provide a precise, step-by-step chemical explanation of the enzymatic reaction that occurs when an onion is sliced? Specifically, I need to explain the pathway from the initial cell rupture to the formation of the volatile lachrymatory factor, propanethial S-oxide, including the roles of alliinase and the relevant sulfoxides. Please keep the explanation focused on the biochemical mechanism for an academic setting.",
